<title>JAPAN: INTERVIEW - MOF says no Japan banks now insolvent.</title>
<headline>INTERVIEW - MOF says no Japan banks now insolvent.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>There are no Japanese banks that are insolvent at present, although there are some insolvent credit unions, Sei Nakai, a deputy director-general at the Ministry of Finance (MOF) banking bureau said on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;It is the banks in the worst business conditions which have gone under. We have liquidated (banks) which had been clearly insolvent,&quot; he said in an interview with Reuters Financial Television.</p>
</text>
